# atomic sandbox replay v1
# M4 "Drag while playing = spring" and fix round 1 I1 (never a teleport while playing): with the
# run playing, a Select-drag of H2's nucleus 0 sends DragStart / DragMove, and the capped spring
# pulls the nucleus; it never jumps to the cursor. The cursor lines 40 ms apart replay the drag
# at its recorded pace (400 ms, a few DFT steps at 49^3 on the GPU). How many steps land under the
# drag depends on the machine, hence the wide range; the cursor ends 3.34 Bohr from nucleus 1,
# where a jump would have put the nucleus.
view 1400 900
action smooth-motion false
action preset h2
wait idle
action tool select
t 100 cursor 0.1043005 0.0244677
action play
wait steps 1
t 200 button left down
t 240 cursor 0.1343005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 280 cursor 0.1643005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 320 cursor 0.1943005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 360 cursor 0.2243005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 400 cursor 0.2543005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 440 cursor 0.2843005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 480 cursor 0.3143005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 520 cursor 0.3443005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 560 cursor 0.3743005 0.0244677
wait ms 40
t 600 cursor 0.4043005 0.0244677
t 610 button left up
wait steps 4
expect dist 0 1 1.0 2.6
expect paused false
action pause
wait idle
expect paused true
expect no-error
